.TH URNETWORK-CONNECT 1 "2026-11-04" "urnetwork-client 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
urnetwork-connect \- start, stop and manage the URnetwork client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B urnetwork-connect
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ command-options ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B on
Replay the last used mode (default
.IR socks ).
.TP
.B help
Print the command list and exit.
.TP
.B socks
Start the SOCKS5 proxy on
.I 127.0.0.1:9999
(no root needed).
.TP
.B vpn
Start the system-wide TUN VPN (needs root; uses sudo).
.TP
.B off
Stop the running engine, remove the TUN device, restore the previous default
route and clean up state.
.TP
.B toggle
Stop the engine if it is running, otherwise replay the last mode.
.TP
.B status
Show the account, which engine is running, the saved mode and the state file.
.TP
.B list-locations
Print the countries and cities offered by the network.
.TP
.B register EMAIL PASSWORD
Register the local account and store the password in the desktop secret store.
Must be run as your normal user, not as root.  The registration step itself
passes the password to the upstream provider binary on its command line.
.TP
.B verify CODE
Verify the account with the code sent by e-mail.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --timeout SECONDS
Stop the engine after the given time (used for tests).
.TP
.B --retry N
How many times to restart a crashed engine (default 3).
.TP
.BI --country " NAME"
Preferred exit country.
.TP
.BI --city " NAME"
Preferred exit city.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/auth
account name and network; the password is kept in the desktop secret store
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/state.json
state of the running engine
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/connect.lock
single-instance lock
.TP
.I ~/.config/urnetwork/default-route.before
saved default route, restored by
.B off
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B USER_AUTH, PASSWORD
credentials; normally loaded from the auth file and the secret store
.TP
.B URNETWORK_CONFIG_DIR
override the configuration directory (honoured in SOCKS mode; in VPN mode the
root copy always uses the invoking user's
.I ~/.config/urnetwork ).
.TP
.B URNETWORK_CREDENTIALS_HELPER
path to the Secret Service helper
.TP
.B URNETWORK_KEYRING
set to
.I 0
to keep the password in the auth file instead of the secret store
.TP
.B URNETWORK_ASKPASS_TIMEOUT
seconds to wait for the sudo password window (default 180)
.TP
.B URNETWORK_FORCE_ASKPASS
set to
.I 1
to always use the askpass window instead of a passwordless sudo rule
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR urnetwork-gui (1),
.BR urnetwork-vpn (1)
